!
! Distance run on a leg (binnacle_rules.h BR6), in Trebago, one leg a row:
! floor(speed * secs / 3600) metres, speed in metres an hour (a knot is
! 1852) and secs the seconds on the leg, each 0 .. 999999. Trebago is
! exact and has no floor, so the floor of p = speed * secs over 3600 is
! counted three digits at a time: each group is the count of k = 1 to 999
! with k * step * 3600 <= p, which min(1, max(0, p - k * step * 3600 + 1))
! is for integers, and p loses what it counted. ok is 0, and the answer
! divided by it refused, for a speed or a time outside its range. Trebago
! answers a run past 99999999 m, which run.sutra refuses as an overflow of
! its picture: held.
trebago leg_run
  in  speed(n), secs(n)
  out run(n)
  var ok(n), p(n), q1(n), q2(n), q3(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, speed(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 1000000 - speed(i))) &
        * min(1, max(0, secs(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 1000000 - secs(i)))
  p(i) = speed(i) * secs(i)
  q1(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, p(i) - k * 3600000000 + 1)))
  p(i) = p(i) - q1(i) * 3600000000
  q2(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, p(i) - k * 3600000 + 1)))
  p(i) = p(i) - q2(i) * 3600000
  q3(i) = sum(k = 1:999, min(1, max(0, p(i) - k * 3600 + 1)))
  run(i) = (q1(i) * 1000000 + q2(i) * 1000 + q3(i)) / ok(i)
end
